# Netlify reads this file from the publish root.
#
# These paths exist so a shared link resolves for everyone. On a device with
# the app installed, iOS matches the URL against the association file and opens
# the app directly — these rules never run. Everywhere else the same URL has to
# land somewhere real, so it forwards to the store.
#
# 302, not 301: the store lives on myshopify.com today. A permanent redirect
# would be cached by browsers and become very hard to take back once these
# paths are served natively.
#
# Deliberately no catch-all. A `/* /index.html 200` rule would swallow
# /.well-known/apple-app-site-association, and universal links fail silently
# when that file returns HTML — nothing is logged, they simply stop working.

/products/*     https://uncharted-tribe-collective.myshopify.com/products/:splat     302
/collections/*  https://uncharted-tribe-collective.myshopify.com/collections/:splat  302
/cart           https://uncharted-tribe-collective.myshopify.com/cart                302
/releases       https://uncharted-tribe-collective.myshopify.com/collections/all     302
/past-runs      https://uncharted-tribe-collective.myshopify.com/collections/all     302
/collective     /find-your-tribe.html                                                302
